{
  "raw": {
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10982": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Administrative Assistant Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Division of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering (CCE) seeks a motivated, adaptable, and intellectually curious individual to join the division’s administrative team. CCE faculty are among the most distinguished and innovative in the world, leading research into new areas of science and technology. Reporting to the Division Operations Officer, the successful candidate will provide tailored administrative support to multiple research groups and professors while working within a dynamic and collaborative team of administrative staff. This individual will interact with various departments and programs on campus and leverage cutting-edge automation and AI tools to support the ambitious goals of Caltech research laboratories. This role offers an exciting opportunity for an individual eager to provide high-level administrative support at a collaborative, world-class research institute. The selected candidate will gain mentorship, skill development, proximity to science, exposure to career pathways, training in research administration, experience with grant proposals, and professional development. The role is a strong fit for someone interested in research administration, academic operations, grants management, science communication, and/or AI-enabled productivity. Essential Job Duties Administrative Support and Coordination: Provide administrative assistance to professors and research groups. Tailor support to individual faculty needs, including managing calendars and scheduling meetings, appointments, and interviews. Answer and compose correspondence on behalf of professors, maintaining a professional and proactive communication style. Document Preparation and Editing: Draft, type, edit, and/or proof manuscripts, patent applications, grant proposals, funding reports, and other documents as needed. Prepare and edit PowerPoint presentations, developing presentation materials from original content. Take ownership of improving templates, workflows, group documentation, and recurring administrative processes. Grant and Budget Management: Track deadlines for grant proposals, ensuring timely submission and compliance with funding agency requirements. Prepare and collate grant proposal supporting sections, including for NIH submissions. Provide budget-related assistance by reconciling discrepancies and tracking purchases. Provide data and input for financial projections, collaborating with grant managers as needed. Event Planning and Coordination: Plan, organize, and coordinate special events such as seminars, symposiums, conferences, and faculty dinners. Coordinate logistics, including speaker travel arrangements, lecture hall AV setup, catering, and budget reconciliation. Teaching Support: Prepare classroom materials, arrange teaching equipment/AV, and collect homework and examinations for undergraduate and graduate courses. Maintain files of letters of recommendation for student and postdoctoral applications. Personnel Coordination: Maintain up-to-date information on research group members. Coordinate interview and hiring processes for new members. Update lab-specific guides and distribute them to new members. AI Integration and Utilization: Learn and implement AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, CoPilot, and other relevant technologies to enhance efficiency in administrative tasks. Use AI and automation tools to assist with drafting documents, managing schedules, creating reports, and streamlining communication and workflows. General Office Management: Maintain records, databases, and document files electronically and in hard copy, ensuring accuracy and confidentiality. Manage purchasing cards, reconcile expenses, and process reimbursements. Interface with campus personnel, external associates, and Division staff, acting as a liaison to the research group(s). Other Duties as Assigned: Provide administrative backup to other administrative staff and assist with Division-wide initiatives as needed. Serve as the Floor Warden or Building Coordinator for emergency planning purposes. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience. 3+ years of administrative support experience, preferably in an academic setting, or equivalent experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and calendaring/email systems. Demonstrated experience using AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, and CoPilot; understanding of when the use of AI tools is or isn’t appropriate, and whether a particular AI output aligns with the prompt and intended purpose. Highly organized, able to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines with accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to interface professionally with faculty, staff, students, and visitors. Strong word-processing and proofreading skills. Ability to work independently, demonstrate good judgment, and maintain confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of Caltech policies, procedures, and systems. Proficient with both PC and Mac operating systems. Previous experience supporting senior faculty and/or managing NIH grant proposals. Experience with workflow automation such as Microsoft 365 automations or similar tools to streamline processes and integrate systems. Experience with content management systems or developing other web-based applications (e.g., research lab websites). Required Documents Resume Cover Letter explaining your interest in supporting research and academic operations, and why you believe your prior experiences make you a strong match for this role. Please include in your letter: (1) any prior experience with workflow automation and/or AI systems, and (2) your views on which top three tasks/responsibilities from the position description would benefit most from using AI/automation tools and why. Limit your cover letter to no more than one page. Hiring Range $20.00 - $33.00 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11008": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Application Developer Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary NExScI at Caltech/IPAC has an opening for an Application Developer with a strong background in Unix software development to join the Keck Observatory Archive (KOA) development team. Come be a part of the team that is helping astronomers and data scientists all over the world access and explore the rich data sets available at KOA. NExScI (nexsci.caltech.edu) provides archive services, community support, science operations, and analysis tools related to the discovery and characterization of planets beyond our solar system (exoplanets) using data from observatories in space and on the ground. You will work with a vibrant team of scientists and developers to prepare for t 2030s when Keck Observatory Archive to ingest and serve massive and complex new data sets delivered by new instruments. This work is part of a broader program to upgrade and modernize the archive infrastructure and provide new user services that respond to the rapid changes in the science analysis landscape. Essential Job Duties As a NExScI Application Developer, you will work with the engineering and scientific team members to develop systems that serve data to archive users. The work will, in part, involve exploring the use of agentic AI to deliver these systems: Support the development of new query infrastructures and end user services that offer fast access to complex data sets. Extending the archive infrastructure to ingest and organize scientific data into the archive. Automating and improving the management of our development environment through improved CI/CM processes within the GitHub repository. Implement systems for software library and OS version controls. Implement logging and metrics for reporting and status monitoring. Streamline deployment of software into test and production environments, through continuous integration, and troubleshoot runtime issues. Basic Qualifications If you have the following in your background, then we want to hear about your interest in joining our team: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, and a minimum of four years of relevant professional or academic experience in modern software engineering. Expertise in Python, Linux/UNIX environments, and shell scripting. Proficiency in AI/ML and experience with modern development and deployment tools, including Docker, Kubernetes, and Jenkins. Knowledge of configuration management practices and tools such as Git/GitHub and Jira. Strong communication, interpersonal, and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively in collaborative environments. Preferred Qualifications These additional qualifications may give you a strong start, though we still encourage you to apply even if you don’t have all of them: Master’s degree in Astronomy, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Sciences, or a related field. Experience with web server administration, operations, and cloud services. Expertise in AI/ML, databases, and SQL. Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and modern cloud-based development environments. Required Documents Full resume Cover letter Contact information for three professional references Life at IPAC People choose to work at IPAC for many reasons, and the casual, employee-centric culture often leads to fulfilling, long-term careers and positive relationships. Caltech’s benefits program offers a quality, competitive benefits package that is affordable for you and the Institute. We also offer a 403(b) defined contribution plan to eligible staff as well as a Voluntary Retirement Savings (TDA) Plan. IPAC staff have access to the Institute’s facilities, including the athletic center, libraries, on-site daycare, professional development and enrichment classes, and Athenaeum club membership. Hiring Range $40.00 - $47.00 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10900": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Diving Job Category Occasional ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Non-Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Diving is responsible for assisting in the coaching and teaching of students, game and practice preparation and execution, compliance with NCAA, and conference rules/regulations. Job Duties Demonstrating a high level of teaching and coaching competency in sport skill instruction, sport strategy, tactics and rules, physical training and fitness and student motivation in practice execution. Demonstrating a sincere interest in the social, emotional, academic development, as well as the athletic welfare of student-athletes; collaborating on academic monitoring and guidance of students where appropriate. Exhibiting the highest professional standards and ethical behavior with regard to adherence to the NCAA, SCIAC Conference, Caltech and the Department of Athletics and Recreation’s values statement, including sportsmanship on and off the field of play, positive leadership and the desire and ability to act as a positive role model and representative of the Institute at all times. Demonstrate excellent communication skills including writing, speaking, and listening. Contributing to the maintenance of excellent working relationships with all members of the Department and promoting the philosophy and objectives of the intercollegiate athletic program on and off campus. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications Must be knowledgeable and skilled in all areas of the sport. Knowledge of SCIAC and NCAA rules and regulations. First Aid and CPR Certification or ability to quickly become certified. Possess, or have the ability to obtain by the date of hire, a valid California Driver's License and maintain it throughout the course of employment. Physical Demands/Work Environment The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Each coaching staff member may be required to perform physical tasks such as: Lifting, carrying, loading sport specific equipment up to 50 lbs. Set up and tear down of sports contest support equipment. Some care and maintenance of sport specific or general athletic facilities. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 2 or more years of relevant experience. Collegiate playing experience. Organized coaching experience. Teaching through digital images; creating and using emerging technologies. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Coaching Philosophy. Hiring Range $20 - $25 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11073": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Director, Stewardship Communications Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The purpose of Advancement and Alumni Relations (AAR) is to foster a thriving and engaged community of support for Caltech. By strengthening and nurturing the community of people who share and support the Institute’s mission and values, we will ensure the Institute receives the necessary resources to achieve our aspirations and advocate for excellence in teaching, research, and scholarship in perpetuity. Reporting to the Associate Director of Stewardship Communications, the Assistant Director performs all aspects of a wide variety of donor relations-related communications projects to inspire continued support for Caltech. The position requires superb writing and editing skills, and the ability to develop materials that acknowledge, promote, celebrate, or convey philanthropic impact.  Typical assignments include writing and designing personalized donor impact reports, reviewing donor recognition pieces, and developing event invitations and program materials. The Assistant Director works closely with teammates in Philanthropic Initiatives and Stewardship, as well as Advancement Communications, colleagues throughout AAR, and members of the academic community. They also interact with senior leaders of the Institute, notably including the vice president for Advancement and Alumni Relations, as well as faculty in all academic divisions. Essential Job Duties Research and write compelling reports and other individualized communications in support of the Institute's significant donors, inspiring continued philanthropy and conveying the impact of giving. Translate complex academic, scientific, and technology-focused concepts into clear, compelling language for educated, non-technical audiences. Independently conduct research and incorporate changes, comments, and critiques from multiple reviewers using exceptional writing and editing skills; exercise sound judgment with regard to strategy and appropriate points of emphasis. Review, edit, and proofread donor stewardship materials, including gift agreements and correspondence. Draft gift acknowledgment templates and other official correspondence (appointment notifications, condolence notes, etc.) for the vice president for Advancement and the provost. Regularly update templates to ensure they reflect the voice and style of the signer. Review event materials (including invitations, menus, programs, etc.) and produce speaking points/remarks and follow-up messages for donor events, as needed. Use graphic design skills to support the creation of Stewardship materials (both print and web-based) including selecting and securing appropriate images, developing layouts, and preparing files for print or digital publication. Collaborate with external graphic designers as needed. Review language for donor recognition pieces and signage that acknowledge and honor the philanthropy of Caltech’s supporters. Manage multiple projects simultaneously and independently and keep a comprehensive plan of all work in progress. Analyze requests for assistance, project realistic deadlines for project completion, and complete work on schedule. Develop strong working relationships and understand the communications goals and styles of other writing teams across campus to ensure the successful integration of donor-stewardship materials with the messaging of Advancement Communications, Strategic Communications, and other academic partners. Collaborate with colleagues in Advancement Communications and the Office of Communications and External Relations to ensure all materials produced align with Institute messaging, tone, style, and brand guidelines. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent related work experience. Three years or more of experience in a professional communications role. Proven superior writing, editing, and proofreading skills. Ability to communicate about a wide range of science and technology topics to non-technical audiences. Ability to synthesize complex information into clear and persuasive prose. Ability to independently manage complex tasks simultaneously, coordinate the roles of various participants in projects, set priorities and schedules, and meet deadlines with minimal supervision. Exceptional attention to detail. Ability to continually seek new ways to tell the story of impact to donors across various channels. Expertise in developing and implementing best practices for conveying impact to donors. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to facilitate mutual understanding and work effectively with a wide variety of people, including faculty, administrators, advancement colleagues, donors, alumni, students, and friends of the Institute. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). Authentic curiosity and interest in science and technology. Demonstrate the ability to practice and uphold AAR’s guiding principles. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree, preferably in English, Journalism or Communications or a related field. Advancement writing experience. Science or medical writing experience is highly desirable. Familiarity with higher education or non-profit environment. Proficiency using Adobe InDesign and the Adobe Creative Suite. Proficiency using digital e-mail platforms, preferably Encompass and Thankview. Understanding of graphic design concepts and ability to positively enhance the design of projects and materials. An understanding of the advancement enterprise—particularly within an academic setting—and the ability to work within that framework. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $78,900 - $106,800 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11076": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Director of Stewardship Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The purpose of Advancement and Alumni Relations (AAR) is to foster a thriving and engaged community of support for Caltech. By strengthening and nurturing the community of people who share and support the Institute's mission and values, we will ensure the Institute receives the necessary resources to achieve our aspirations and advocate for excellence in teaching, research, and scholarship in perpetuity. Reporting to the Director of Stewardship, the Assistant Director of Stewardship is charged with supporting Caltech’s comprehensive donor-centric stewardship program, which enhances the donor experience through accurate and consistent stewardship reporting. The Assistant Director possesses exceptional organizational skills, high attention to detail, an ability to meet deadlines, and a strong commitment to customer service. Partnering with other members of the Stewardship team, the Assistant Director helps ensure the long-term sustainability of Caltech’s donor stewardship efforts by maintaining accurate data, mastering internal reporting processes, and creating additional efficiencies within the unit’s reporting systems. Essential Job Duties Regularly audit new gift fund records, as well as systematically review older fund records, to preserve Stewardship’s data integrity through consistent data collection and regular maintenance and enhancement of information within the AAR database. Run reports and provide relevant data for the team’s centralized, annual fund stewardship reporting activities for more than 700 endowed and current-use funds. Help request and compile content for stewardship reports, such as student questionnaire responses for scholarship and fellowship reports. Manage data within the ThankView system to facilitate the collection and distribution of stewardship videos from scholars, fellows, and other members of the campus community. Compile information for and facilitate mass uploads of scholarship recipient, fellowship recipient, and endowed fund financial data to the AAR database. Maintain a comprehensive inventory of endowed professorship and leadership chair faculty appointments at Caltech; provide regular updates to Faculty Records, the Provost’s office, and Fund Accounting. Work collaboratively with Advancement Information team and stewardship colleagues to track donor gifts and monitor, maintain, and regularly update information about giving society members and stewardship preferences. Help coordinate e- and hard copy mailings of donor impact reports and other donor stewardship efforts. Maintain gift fund data and the highest level of confidentiality and discretion necessary when working with financial and gift information. Working with stewardship team members, support the tracking of data for individualized stewardship strategies and plans for major donors. This includes: Preparing donor data for stewardship team and prospect manager review. Tacking donor stewardship milestones such as birthdays and anniversaries of significant donor-funded centers, institutes, and related initiatives. Support the daily processing of gift acknowledgment correspondence, as needed. Support generation of gift agreements, as needed. Provide outstanding customer service to AAR colleagues and other internal stakeholders regarding inquiries about annual stewardship reporting activities. In conjunction with stewardship colleagues, proactively identify and resolve issues that impede the fulfillment of donor intent or provide information to campus partners that provides clarity to donor intent. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent related work experience. Three years or more of experience in a nonprofit or higher education setting, with progressive responsibilities in administrative support, data management, and project coordination. Experience with the philosophy and practices of institutional advancement and the principles of donor stewardship. Excellent organizational, time management, and project management skills; ability to work collaboratively as well as manage projects proactively and independently to completion with limited oversight. Meticulous attention to detail and accuracy. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other programs that provide the ability to interpret, manage, and track large quantities of data. Experience using business databases to maintain and extract data. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including outstanding proofreading skills; ability to communicate effectively and efficiently with co-workers and the campus wide community. Demonstrated ability to handle confidential information with discretion. Strong customer service orientation and skills, demonstrating a professional and friendly demeanor, including the ability to anticipate and provide helpful service to internal and external customers. Ability to articulate process and procedures in order to support and train others. Authentic curiosity about science and technology. Demonstrate the ability to practice and adhere to AAR’s Guiding Principles. Preferred Qualifications Proficiency with Ellucian’s Advance advancement and alumni relations database software or similar CRM. Experience with other applications/tools such as Encompass, ThankView, InDesign, or other donor stewardship technologies. Experience with SharePoint, Power Automate, and/or some basic coding skills a plus. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $68,400 - $104,000 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11049": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Finance & Operations Coordinator Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Finance & Operations in Student Affairs (AVP), and with the guidance of the Senior Finance Coordinator, the Assistant Finance Coordinator supports multiple processes within Caltech Student Auxiliary Services (SAS). Responsibilities include working with outside vendors, Payment Services, Financial Services, and other Caltech departments to coordinate procurement, payment, billing, credit card settlement, and accounting processes. Essential Job Duties In cooperation with Institute Finance, responsible for ensuring the accurate booking of thousands of internal and external SAS revenue transactions per month. Administers and tracks procurement and accounts payables processes for all SAS business units (Housing, Dining, Retail), as well as some Student Affairs (SAO) units. Assists in development, implementation, and documentation of other business processes, and ensures compliance with relevant Institute policies and procedures. Works with the Senior Finance Coordinator to complete monthly journal entries, e.g. cost of sales and cash accruals. Works with managers to ensure timely procurement of services and materials necessary for business operations. Provides excellent customer service for all customers and vendor partners. Supports processes for internal and external customer billing, and addresses customer and vendor billing inquiries. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or higher in business, accounting, information systems, or related discipline, or equivalent years of education and/or work experience. 1 year of related experience. Experience with accounting, billing and financial reporting processes. Problem solving skills and ability to interface with diverse populations. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong organizational and multi-tasking skills. Demonstrated excellent customer service skills. Ability to interact with all levels of campus personnel. Proficiency with MS Office suite. Ability to work occasional nights and weekends during periods of high demand. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Techmart (SciQuest), CardQuest, Oracle and data warehouse tools is a plus. Previous higher education experience is a plus. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Hiring Range $30.50 - $34.75 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11061": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Business Systems Consultant Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Reporting to the Facilities Information Systems Manager, the Associate Business Systems Consultant will be part of a small team responsible for the following: Design, implement, enhance and maintain solutions for Facilities business applications (IWMS AiM, ArcGIS, Power BI models, and other applications. Utilize best business practices, perform tasks such as gathering requirements, identifying/evaluating software and solutions that meet the needs of Facilities and the Campus community. Coordinate, analyze, and develop systems and/or processes, which are cost effective and meet user requirements. Troubleshooting issues within Facilities business applications and working with the Support teams to resolve issues. Working with key technology partners, develop and sustain Caltech’s digital twin model and associated management tools, SkySpark, etc. Essential Job Duties Provides a full range of Information Systems Services including implementation of new applications/modules, Power BI/SQL programming, user support, data management, and training. Participates in the entire lifecycle of a system which includes but is not limited to gathering requirements, analyzing, planning, design, configuration, testing, deployment, roll out and maintenance. Works with the customer to facilitate negotiating, and capture requirements for enterprise and/or standalone applications. Creates and modifies software training documentation and works with users to understand Facilities software systems. Independently perform data validation and module testing. Provides consultation to system users on technical and/or functional issues. Analysis of situations or data requires identification, review and interpretation of policies, procedures and practices. Troubleshoots and resolves customer inquiries effectively. Exercises judgment and discretion in applying applicable policies and procedures to situations and significant problems. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience with at least four years of related experience Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite of applications. Working knowledge of Power BI, SQL, DAX, R, and Power Query (M) with experience developing reports, dashboards, data models, and business intelligence solutions. Experience developing Power BI dashboards and data models to support business reporting and operational decision-making. Experience in creating and maintaining business process documentation, training materials, and reporting solutions to support system users and continuous improvement initiatives. Must have implementation experience. Demonstrated problem-solving skills, and supportive and team-oriented. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Collaborative work style and ability to adapt to changes in priorities, assignments, and more. Proven ability to adapt vendor-provided documentation and train customers in the use of software Ability to take personal initiative and leverage problem-solving skills to figure out how business software functions and how it interfaces with other applications. Must be able to support the evaluation, implementation, testing, and adoption of business applications and AI-enabled solutions to improve operational efficiency, data accessibility, and decision-making. Demonstrated ability to utilize AI and automation to reduce manual processes, improve data quality, and enhance decision support capabilities. Experience assisting with system configuration, user acceptance testing (UAT), data validation, troubleshooting, and end-user training to support successful application deployments. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Business Analytics. Experience in higher education. Experience supporting initiatives for a large, complex facility. Experience conducting software quality assurance testing. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $49.00 - $57.75 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11090": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Dean of Graduate Studies Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Associate Dean of Graduate Studies reports to the Dean of Graduate Students and plays a core leadership role in shaping the academic and personal development of graduate students. This position is responsible for student well-being both in and out of the classroom, addressing a broad spectrum of issues, including academic and personal advising and support services, faculty outreach and communication, student conduct, and crisis management. This position requires significant collaboration across multiple campus offices, including Student Wellness Services, the Center for Inclusion and Diversity, Equity and Title IX, the Registrar, Housing, the Office of Student and Family Engagement, and the Option managers and representatives. The Associate Dean leads and manages student academic programs and partnerships to enhance the graduate experience and ensure academic success and personal well-being. This role also requires the development of new initiatives and student support systems that respond to emerging needs. Finally, the Associate Dean serves as the senior-most staff member in the Graduate Office, providing high-level vision, leadership, and strategic planning for student academic support and personal development initiatives. This is an Essential Reporting position. In the event of a campus emergency, an employee designated as Essential Reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery and is expected to report to Campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Program Development: Build, implement, and manage student support programs. Develop and present academic components of new student orientation, and new academic interventions. Continually assess and enhance these programs to adapt to evolving student needs. Collaboration and Networking: Forge strong partnerships across campus with student support services, faculty, and administrative offices to promote student success. Actively maintain a wide network of relationships to ensure comprehensive support for students, leveraging resources from various campus departments and external partners. Student Advising: With a deep understanding of academic policies and procedures, provide high-level academic and personal advising to graduate students. This includes coordinating with faculty, academic advisors in the Divisions, residential life staff, and other offices to support students facing academic or personal challenges. Advise students on academic petitions, leaves of absence, reinstatements, and other academic needs. Admissions: In conjunction with the Assistant Dean, maintains a foundational understanding and awareness of the decentralized graduate admissions process. Maintains open communication with Division and Option representatives to ensure the process runs smoothly and stakeholders’ needs are met. Crisis Management: Respond to student crises in collaboration with Student Wellness Services, Campus Security, Equity and Title IX, and other relevant departments. Play a pivotal role in Caltech’s CARE team, which provides case management for students experiencing challenges. Participate in the Student Affairs on-call rotation system. Student Conduct: Oversee student conduct, investigate conduct cases, and make recommendations of disciplinary action to the Dean. Account and Budget Management: Administer the student emergency fund and other discretionary funds overseen by the Dean of Graduate Studies. In consultation with the Dean and Financial Analyst, manage the office’s general budget and operations spending. Committee Involvement: Serve on campus committees at the direction of the Dean. Act as the Dean’s representative as required. Serve as a liaison to the Graduate Student Council (GSC) and advise graduate student leaders. Leadership role: Play a leadership role for the graduate office staff and represent the office. Policy Development: Develop and implement policies and procedures that enhance the student experience. Assess and improve academic policies and Dean’s office procedures to address changing student needs. Union Relations and Compliance: Work in collaboration with the Labor Relations team to provide guidance and recommendations to academic leadership on a wide range of matters including the application and interpretation of academic policies, Institute policy and procedures, union contract provisions, labor agreements, and related regulatory requirements. Ensure that the articles of the collective bargaining agreement are applied uniformly across the academic Divisions; conduct trainings and periodic reviews of compliance. Grievances and Investigations: Fill a key role in the grievance and appeals process outlined in the collective bargaining agreement. Conduct complex and sensitive investigations with little supervision, including determining appropriate investigation strategies, leading witness interviews and any required document review, and determining findings and recommendations for appropriate resolution. Special Projects: Execute high-impact projects at the request of the Dean, often involving collaboration with various stakeholders and departments. Basic Qualifications Master's degree. 5 years of increasingly responsible experience in student affairs. Excellent leadership and managerial skills and the capacity to supervise a team of professionals. Excellent counseling and advising skills, the ability to utilize independent judgment in a fair, consistent manner. Exceptional analytical and organizational skills, excellent communication skills, a strong service orientation, and an ability to exercise independent judgment while working in a team-oriented environment. Ability to build strong collaborations with other offices. Strong communication skills, both verbal and written. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate degree. Experience in crisis management. Administrative experience, work in higher education, supervisory experience, academic management experience or equivalent. A demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusivity. Previous Caltech experience. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $146,600 - $180,100 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11096": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Director, JPL International Office Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Reporting to the Director of the International Offices, the Associate Director will be responsible for supervising the day-to-day operation of the JPL International Office (JPL IO); and for doing direct advising and preparation of immigrant and nonimmigrant documents and petitions.  This position strategizes with the Director in the development of JPL policy and procedure on immigration issues for scholars and students. The staff members of the International Offices at Caltech and JPL work as a team.  Advisors consult with one another in order to maintain consistent immigration advising for Caltech and JPL, and support each other when necessary. Essential Job Duties Supervisory Supervise JPL IO staff, includes assigning tasks monitoring the day-to-day activities; leading team meetings; providing individual staff feedback, guidance, and support; providing training and professional development opportunities; and leading annual performance reviews Develop office policies and procedures; initiate and direct improvements Manage maintenance of efficient and uniform practices Oversee and analyze regular reports for operational audits and data integrity Oversee and manage communications – including email templates, website, web forms, and flyers – with international scholars, as well as internal and external partners for consistency of message, voice, design, and content Develop innovative, compliant, and enriching orientation for international scholars and students Develop international education outreach for lab community and lab business partners Collaborate and consult regularly with Associate Directors for International Student Programs (ISP) and International Scholar Services (ISS) Establish and maintain relationships with JPL IO lab business partners to educate, collaborate and assist in the service of institutional compliance and the international student and scholar experience Provide project management leadership and contributions to system implementations Scholar and Student Advising Provide direct immigration advising to international students and scholars from pre-arrival to departure; prepare E-3, H, TN, O, and green card petitions; prepare F and J documents, as needed; support F-1 OPT/STEM OPT, as appropriate Serve as Alternate Responsible Office (ARO) for Caltech’s J Exchange Visitor Program and as a Designated School Official (DSO) for Caltech’s F Student program Stay current on changing immigration laws, regulations, and policy; interpret and apply to internal business practices Prepare and file petitions, applications, and correspondence with the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS), the U.S. Department of Labor (DOL), and U.S. Department of State (DOS) Strategize and coordinate with outside immigration counsel, when appropriate. Provide timely updates and presentations to international students and scholars and JPL IO lab business partners regarding immigration changes and business practices Work within ISSM/Trilby and SEVIS; comply with DHS, DOL, and DOS regulations and maintain record keeping Other duties, as assigned Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree 6 years of relevant international scholar or U.S. immigration advising experience, covering both nonimmigrant and immigrant categories 2 years of direct management of administrative and professional staff in an international scholar or U.S. immigration environment Demonstrated ability to initiate efficient and effective business practices and procedures Communication and presentation skills Critical thinking and organizational skills including policy analysis, evaluation of compliance issues, formulation and implementation of internal business procedures, and completion of complex projects in a timely manner In accordance with 22 CFR §62, the individual in this position must be a citizen or lawful permanent resident of the United States Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree Experience working with complex, system-wide databases Experience with the culture, procedures and practices of higher education/research environment Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Hiring Range $102,000 - $124,000 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11109": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Director of Annual Giving Content and Communications Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The purpose of Advancement and Alumni Relations (AAR) is to foster a thriving and engaged community of support for Caltech. By strengthening and nurturing the community of people who share and support the Institute’s mission and values, we will ensure the Institute receives the necessary resources to achieve our aspirations and advocate for excellence in teaching, research, and scholarship in perpetuity. Reporting to the Director of Annual Giving Programs, the Associate Director of Annual Giving Content and Communications leads the Caltech Fund’s integrated content and communications strategy across fundraising, stewardship, and donor engagement initiatives. This position oversees content development across multiple channels, including but not limited to direct mail, email, web, social media, SMS, and emerging digital channels. This role will ensure consistency in voice, messaging, and brand standards across all Caltech Fund communications. The Associate Director of Content and Communications serves as the Caltech Fund’s lead writer and multichannel communications strategist, partnering with colleagues across Advancement and Alumni Relations (AAR) and the broader campus to translate fundraising priorities into compelling donor, student, and campus stories and communications. Working collaboratively with campus partners, stakeholders, and creative freelancers, this role manages concurrent communication initiatives, guiding projects from concept through production while ensuring the timely delivery of high-quality communications that advance fundraising goals and institutional priorities. Essential Job Duties Write, edit, and produce original written content for Annual Giving fundraising, stewardship, and engagement campaigns, translating fundraising strategies into compelling donor communications across print and digital channels. Develop and oversee comprehensive multichannel content marketing and communications strategies that drive revenue growth and support the Caltech Fund’s fundraising, stewardship, and donor engagement goals. Develop and manage the Caltech Fund’s messaging strategy, ensuring consistency in voice, messaging, editorial standards, and brand across all fundraising communications. Own the development and production schedules of Caltech Fund fundraising and stewardship communications, including but not limited to direct mail appeals, email campaigns, website content, social media, SMS, and other donor-facing communications. Manage multiple simultaneous communication campaign schedules against hard deadlines with specific audience goals and objectives. Partner with the Annual Giving Specialist to identify, interview, track, and create compelling stories sourced from the work of Caltech’s students, faculty, and campus community. Develop and implement new digital engagement tools and strategies while managing the Caltech Fund’s website content, social media presence, SMS, and other digital communication channels. Partner with the Associate Director of Annual Giving Data, Reporting, and Analytics to analyze campaign performance and engagement metrics and recommend improvements to communications strategy and donor engagement. Collaborate with colleagues across Advancement and Alumni Relations (AAR) and the broader Institute to identify communications opportunities, source donor and student stories, coordinate messaging, and support integrated fundraising initiatives. Identify and recommend industry trends, best practices, and performance-driven improvements to strengthen fundraising solicitations and donor engagement. Manage relationships with freelance graphic designers, writers, photographers, and other creative contractors, including coordinating deliverable, maintaining quality standards, and ensuring projects remain on schedule. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent related work. Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in communications, content strategy, marketing, public relations, or related fields, with demonstrated success. developing integrated, multi-channel communications. Demonstrated experience leading integrated communications strategies and multi-channel campaigns. Exceptional writing, editing, and project management skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams). Working knowledge of Adobe applications, especially Acrobat, InDesign, and Photoshop. Enthusiasm, passion, and curiosity about higher education development and nonprofit fundraising. Authentic curiosity about science and technology. Demonstrate the ability to practice and adhere to AAR’s Guiding Principles. Preferred Qualifications Experience in an annual giving, advancement, or a comparable nonprofit fundraising environment, including the development and production of print communications such as direct mail solicitations and brochures Experience developing integrated fundraising communications and donor engagement strategies within higher education advancement or a comparable nonprofit fundraising environment. Experience in fundraising communications, annual giving campaigns, donor engagement strategies, or nonprofit storytelling. Experience with project management software (such as Smart Sheet, Asana, Monday, Workfront, Basecamp, or equivalent tools). Experience managing content and communications freelancers or cross-functional project teams. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $100,700 - $137,500 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11100": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Director of Undergraduate Admissions & STARS Program Director Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Associate Director of Undergraduate Admissions & STARS Program Director is a key member of the Access, Analytics, and Recruitment team within Caltech’s Undergraduate Admissions Office. Reporting directly to the Senior Associate Director, this role serves as a strategic partner in advancing the Institute’s recruitment, access, and enrollment goals. This position provides leadership across two primary areas: (1) supporting the strategic direction and day-to-day operations of the Access, Analytics, and Recruitment team, including supervision and mentorship of staff, and (2) serving as the Program Director for the STARS College Network program, leading Caltech’s efforts to recruit, support, and enroll talented students from rural and small-town backgrounds. The Associate Director plays a critical role in shaping data-informed recruitment strategies, guiding team initiatives, and ensuring alignment with institutional priorities. As a senior member of the team, this individual contributes to staff training, and cross-functional collaboration, while also serving as an Admissions Officer responsible for territory management, application review, and student engagement. Essential Job Duties Leadership & Team Management Serve as a strategic partner and primary support to the Senior Associate Director in advancing team priorities and initiatives. Provide direct supervision, mentorship, and professional development for two Senior Assistant Directors, ensuring strong project execution and staff growth. Guide and support team members in developing, implementing, and assessing recruitment and access initiatives. Help set team priorities, workflows, and performance expectations in alignment with office and institutional goals. Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing team environment. STARS Program Leadership (Primary Functional Area) Serve as Caltech’s Program Director and primary liaison to the STARS College Network and associated partners. Lead the strategy, development, and execution of all rural and small-town student recruitment initiatives. Manage and oversee all STARS-related programming, including outreach, engagement, yield efforts, and partnership development. Conducts analysis on effectiveness of territorial outreach programs, reports outcomes, and makes recommendations on strategies. Plans and executes domestic campaigns targeting rural and small-town high school students, parents, and counselors. Develop and maintain relationships with high schools, community-based organizations, and national partners supporting rural college access. Represent Caltech in STARS network meetings, working groups, and national collaborations. Oversee program budget, planning, and assessment; evaluate outcomes and recommend improvements. Admissions Officer Responsibilities Manage a designated recruitment territory, including travel, high school visits, and relationship-building with counselors and CBOs. Represent Caltech through information sessions, events, and communications with prospective students and families. Read and evaluate applications within a highly selective admissions process and participate fully in committee deliberations. Support yield efforts, including outreach to admitted students and programming. Support special projects and initiatives as assigned by senior leadership. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent. A minimum of 5 years of experience of experience working a data-oriented field, selective college admissions or higher education. A valid driver’s license is required or equivalent means of reliable transportation to off-site meetings and events. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree is preferred. Experience working with underserved students in an institution of higher education, high school setting, or community-based organization. Proficiency in using CRM systems, particularly Technolutions Slate. Required Documents Resume. CL. Hiring Range $80,000 - $96,200 Per Year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11054": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Video, Multimedia, and Event Specialist Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Caltech Academic Media Technologies (AMT) is a film production and event support team providing innovative, creative, and technical solutions for Caltech’s mission-critical efforts in research, education, and outreach. AMT’s activities include: creating videos and broadcasts for education, outreach, promotion, news, fundraising, stewardship, and internal and external communications; supporting in-person, hybrid, and virtual events for the Board of Trustees, Office of Community and External Relations, academic divisions, campus clients, and JPL; and providing technology, tools, and training for teaching and learning. This position resides in a fast-paced environment and requires strong technical and creative skills in film and event production, broadcasting, educational technology, graphic design, and audio-visual support. The ability to work with the AMT team, campus clients, and vendors is critical for success. Job Duties Assist in all aspects of video and audio production for documentary style filming including setting up, cabling, and operating 4k studio production gear, GoPro video cameras, microphones, audio mixing boards, lights, green screens, and other relevant equipment and software. Record video and audio of live events using 4k studio cameras, microphones, audio mixing boards, and other relevant equipment and software. Set up and operate live streaming hardware and software for Caltech broadcast channels including YouTube. Edit video and audio footage and encode for various deliverables such as media for YouTube, social media, podcasts, and live events. Create graphics for video and event productions in several media formats. Provide technical event support for hybrid meetings using Teams and Zoom meetings, Room, and webinar platforms, including customizing event registration pages and audience surveys, and generating post-event reports and summaries. Mix live audio and perform post-production audio sweetening. Assist in supporting the video and multimedia for Caltech’s online course initiatives including: training the instructors and staff how to audio, video, and screen record; supporting the recordings; editing and uploading content; and troubleshooting the online course platform. Craft audio-visual solutions for events with campus clients requiring site visits, audio-visual problem solving, vendor coordination, and preparing quotes and invoices. Coordinate with external vendors for documentary and live-event productions. Setup and maintain audio-visual equipment for events including cameras, microphones, mixing boards, projectors, speakers, amplifiers, projectors, and related audio-visual equipment for events. Provide computer and device support during meetings, conferences, and lectures. Propose solutions to problems with high energy and a positive attitude and commitment to continual improvement. Meet deadlines within a fast-paced environment. Work with flexibility, efficiency, enthusiasm, tenacity, and diplomacy both individually and as part of a team. Demonstrate commitment to diversity and inclusion of varying views, including the ability to interface with people at all levels at Caltech. Maintain a high level of quality control through reviewing, editing, and proofing own work and work of others. Remain abreast of relevant industry trends, best practices, and emerging technologies, and effectively apply this knowledge to all aspects of the position. Perform work in accordance with Institute and regulatory agencies (e.g. OSHA, ADA) safety standards and practices. Keep track of hours worked on projects, events, and tasks, including generating quotes and invoices. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree with at least 7 years of related experience. Ability to set up and operate audio-visual and recording equipment such as 4k studio and documentary video cameras and accessories such as stabilizers, glide cams, and sliders; audio boards, microphones, amplifiers, and speakers; live broadcasting encoders and equipment; teleprompters; and other relevant equipment. High-skill and attention to detail in live event filming. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite (AfterEffects, Photoshop, Premiere, Illustrator, Media Encoder, Encore, Audition), Pro Tools, Davinci Resolve, Wirecast, Zoom, Teams, OBS, and similar production tools. Excellent organizational communication (verbal and written) and interpersonal skills. Ability to work calmly under pressure and present an attitude of attentiveness, courtesy, and professionalism when dealing with other team members, trustees, faculty, administration, staff, post-doctoral scholars, students, community, visiting speakers, and event patrons. Working knowledge of various computer software (Microsoft Office Suite, Adobe Creative Suite, Zoom, Adobe Acrobat Pro) and operating systems (Mac, Windows, and iOS). Exceptional customer service skills. Ability to work as a team member on a variety of projects. Ability to lift and carry up to 40 pounds. Ability to bend in all directions, squeeze with arms and hands, crawl under furniture, climb stairs, and work outdoors in all kinds of weather. Ability to push and pull rolling items such as carts and camera cases. Ability to distinguish colors and differences in brightness on monitors. Ability to maintain camera image focus. Ability to be directed on camera via headset. Effective and tenacious problem-solving skills. Must be available to work overtime, evenings, and weekends. Must possess a valid California Driver's License. Must be able to adhere to the Institute's driving policy. Preferred Qualifications Master of Fine Arts degree in film, cinematography, animation, media studies, or related field of study. Experience in the following: Film production and audio-visual support in a university setting. Lecture hall and auditorium operations. Online course and learning management platforms such as Canvas. Experience with setting up or using a Digital Asset Management system including NAS video storage. Innate interest and excitement for research and science a plus. Sense of humor a plus. Hiring Range $33.50 to $37.25 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11111": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Athenaeum General Manager Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Job Summary The Athenaeum General Manager serves as the leader and visionary for Caltech’s private membership club for faculty, students, staff and community members.  This individual directs and provides strategic oversight and leadership to overall club operations and various departments within The Athenaeum.  The General Manager is accountable for the club’s budget planning, revenues and cost controls, marketing, staff training and development, and fundraising.  Most importantly, the General Manager ensures that every member’s experience reflects the Athenaeum's tradition of excellence and its role in fostering connection across the Caltech community. Essential Job Duties Leadership and Administrative Accountability: Provide strategic leadership and broad direction to all departments within The Athenaeum, including fiscal operations, hotel operations, membership and marketing, food and beverage, culinary, purchasing, and private and club events. Oversee the planning, development, formulation, and implementation of specific operational policies, programs, procedures, communications strategies, and business plans. Establish, implement, communicate, and reinforce the overall philosophy, mission, and vision of the club as these relate to Institute goals and as established by the Board of Governors, House Committee, and the Vice President for Administration and Chief Operating Officer. Ensure the delivery of the highest quality products, services, programs, and support to all members and their guests, and to campus divisions and departments. Collaborate and work in partnership with the various Committees (Board of Governors, House, Membership, Food, Finance, Design Review, Wine, and the Athenaeum Architectural Preservation Fund) to communicate the current financial or operational state of the club; provide information, advice, and recommendations on policy revisions or creation.  Work with ad hoc committees when these are created by the Board of Governors or the House Committee. Consistently assure that the club is operated in accordance with all applicable local, state, and federal laws through regular renewals of pertinent business licenses, permits, and certifications. Provide broad direction for high-profile events with significant visibility and impact on the reputation of the Institute (i.e., trustee events, social media functions, etc.). Develop and maintain strong working relationships, alliances, and open communications with the entire Caltech community. Fiscal: Formulate annual operating and capital budgets and business plans; work closely with the management team to create these budgets. Continuously evaluate existing sources of revenues and identify and develop new revenue streams from current services and amenities to ensure operational integrity and continuity of the organization. Oversee and review management reports and financial statements with special attention to revenue generation and cost containment; execute corrective action when revenue streams decrease and/or when costs escalate disproportionally with income. Collaborate with the club’s senior team to establish and monitor appropriate controls and safeguards that have been put into place to protect the inflow of cash payments and revenues. Human Resources: Make key decisions on hiring and terminations, promotions, salary changes, training and development, goal setting, and performance evaluations and assessments. Cultivate a positive and productive workplace through communication, vision, teamwork, and commitment. Advance, develop, and improve human resource assets through staff education and training, coaching and counseling of staff as necessary. Facility Management / Infrastructure: Oversee the care and maintenance of the club’s physical assets and facilities; review and provide overall direction and recommendations to the Design Review and House Committees on major construction, renovation/refurbishment, and maintenance projects regarding interior design, materials, supplies, equipment, and services. Create and monitor renovation and construction budgets to ensure that any decisions made are within the project’s finances and resources. Marketing/Communications: Act as the primary communicator for all information, written or oral, to club members and staff. Oversee member relations programs that promote The Athenaeum’s services and facilities to current members; build and shape campaign and outreach programs to potential members; provide vision and guidance to the management team in establishing and initiating events that will attract the participation of all member segments. Oversee the development and implementation of an effective communication and marketing strategy through existing social media platforms. Provide oversight for the concept design and production of communication/collateral materials that shape The Athenaeum’s image among members, prospects, and the community at large. Direct the development and maintenance of The Athenaeum’s website.  Oversee regular email blasts and the publication of the monthly newsletter. Maintain membership within the Club Management Association of America and other professional associations as appropriate; attend conferences, workshops, and meetings to keep abreast of current market trends in the club industry. Fundraising: Expand The Athenaeum Architectural Preservation Fund (AAPF) into a robust sum that will finance the club’s capital and maintenance projects and guarantee the vibrancy and life of the club’s facilities, fixtures, equipment, and collection of artwork. Work with Advancement to develop, establish, and implement a strategic plan in attracting and involving current and prospective donors to the AAPF. Community Outreach: Participate in outside activities/events to enhance the prestige of the club and broaden the scope of the club’s operations by fulfilling the public obligations of the club as a participating member of the community. Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, business, or related field; or equivalent years of relevant work experience. 10+ years of hospitality leadership experience. Established experience in a private club, luxury hotel, resort, or historic property with oversight of multi-department operations. Proven success overseeing hotel and private club financials including operating and capital budgets, member dues models, food, beverage, and events performance, and other related KPIs. Proven experience working with Boards, Trustees, or governance committees, including regular reporting and strategic collaboration. Track record of strategic planning, and organizational leadership. Experience leading high-touch service environments focused on exceptional member and guest experiences. Demonstrated success leading digital marketing, social media, and brand repositioning initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Hospitality Management, Business, or related field. Experience in higher education. Experience managing a historic hotel, luxury membership club, or heritage property with preservation considerations. Certified Club Manager (CCM), Certified Hotel Administrator (CHA), Certified Hospitality Professional (CHP), or other relevant professional credentials. Active involvement in professional associations such as CMAA or AHLA. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $193,000 - $225,000 per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11112": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page This job has moved or is no longer available. Please search our current job openings ."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10912": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Barista - Red Door Marketplace Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Looking for a non-stop and exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands on, and round-the-clock. If you have a great team work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge & innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates four dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, and Avery Kitchen) for a campus community of 2000. We also serve over 850 students, 7 days a week, through our Board Program and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. Under the direction of the unit manager, this position requires minimal supervision with speed and proficiency in all areas of café food and beverage services. This position requires experience working in a high-volume café or food facility. Quickly prepares and assembles beverages according to recipe using commercial espresso equipment. Must have some food knowledge and the willingness to learn. Must be versatile, flexible, with the successful ability to work at any location, preparing beverages, serving food, bussing tables, and restocking station and store items as needed. This position should expect location shifts according to business needs and will be required to learn how to assemble and serve food items according to assembly instructions. Is responsible for set-up and maintenance of an organized, clean, and sanitized food and beverage station at all times. Performs work in accordance with Institute and regulatory agencies safety standards and practice and performs all job duties as assigned. A positive, can-do attitude and team work ethic are a must. The candidate must also be flexible, resourceful, and be able to take ownership & initiative in any given task. This is an Essential Reporting position. An employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery, and is expected to report to campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Prepare and serve espresso and other drinks. Greet customers, ring up orders, and serve pastries and food. Bus plates, cups, glasses, silverware, serving items, etc. Cleans and restocks unit at end of service. Stock condiment station, keeping it clean and organized at all times; restock as needed. Clean seating/service/work areas and equipment, keeping it organized at all times. Maintain maximum standards of sanitation and safety. Work cooperatively as a team member to assist other team members as needed. Provide great customer service daily. Cultivates a positive and productive workplace through communication, teamwork and ownership. Greet and serve all guests in a professional, genuine, and friendly manner. May be required to work some non-shift days, extended shifts, and over-time. May temporarily work a different shift due to unforeseen events or seasonal high volume event needs. Must be able to confront a challenge or adverse situation with calm, resolve, and an open, can-do attitude and positive mindset. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required or assigned. Basic Qualifications Customer service oriented. Experience in the food service industry. Experience as a barista. Ability to communicate fluently and provide direction and guidance to other staff members. Ability to take direction, remember duties, and prioritize assignments. Ability to work congenially and as a team with other staff members, student staff and customers. Ability to carry a minimum of 50 lbs. The selected candidates must pass a pre-employment background investigation and post-offer physical examination to be hired for this position. Selected candidate must maintain attendance and arrive on time for all shifts. Must possess a food handler’s certificate or ability to obtain one by the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. 2+ years working in a fast-paced, team environment. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $19.25 - $20.00 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10927": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Bartender Job Category Parttime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Bartender is responsible for delivering exceptional beverage service in a refined, member-focused environment. This role prepares and presents alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages with precision and consistency, maintains elevated bar operations, and contributes to a seamless, high-touch member experience. The Bartender upholds the highest standards of professionalism, cleanliness, and service excellence. Essential Job Duties Prepare and serve cocktails, wine, beer, and non-alcoholic beverages in accordance with established standards Maintain a clean, organized, and fully stocked bar at all times Maintain draft beer system, including troubleshooting issues, changing kegs, and replacing gas cylinders as needed Prepare fresh ingredients and garnishes, ensuring quality, consistency, and alignment with cocktail program standards Prepare fresh juices, syrups, and other house-made ingredients for cocktail production Produce large-format ice and monitor inventory levels to ensure consistent availability for service Operate bar television and house audio systems, including selecting channels, prioritizing live sporting events, and ensuring systems are turned on and off as needed for service Monitor inventory levels and assist with requisitioning and restocking all bar products and supplies, including liquor, wine, beer, soft drinks, juices, fresh ingredients, garnishes, and paper goods Assists with and participates in monthly inventory counts. Follow proper opening and closing procedures, including cash handling, credit card processing, and reconciliation of chits Ensure responsible alcohol service and compliance with all applicable laws and club policies Maintain strong working knowledge of an ample beverage program, including wines by the glass, beer selections, and a diverse spirits portfolio Provide recommendations and engage with members to enhance the guest experience Coordinate with service staff and management to ensure timely and accurate beverage service Maintain cleanliness and sanitation standards for bar areas, equipment, and glassware Verify pool tables, foosball table, and dart board are in proper working order and ready for use Assist with setup and service for special events and private functions Flex between bartender and server roles based on business needs, maintaining consistent service standards and supporting overall floor operations Report maintenance issues, inventory shortages, or operational concerns to management Perform other duties as assigned Basic Qualifications Minimum 2–3 years of bartending experience, preferably in a high-end restaurant, hotel, or private club Knowledge of classic cocktails, spirits, wine, and beer Ability to multitask and work efficiently in a fast-paced environment Strong communication and customer service skills Ability to lift and carry 85 lbs, and move kegs and bar stock as needed Basic math and cash handling skills Must meet all legal requirements for alcohol service Must possess a valid California Responsible Beverage Service (RBS) certification Must possess a valid California Food Handler Card Preferred Qualifications Experience with craft cocktail programs and fresh ingredient preparation Familiarity with POS systems Wine, beer and spirits knowledge (certifications a plus) Experience in private clubs or fine dining environments Required Documents Resume Hiring Range $23.00 - $34.00 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11116": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Budget Director Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The California Institute of Technology, a private, not-for-profit Research University located in Pasadena, California, seeks a highly motivated, experienced Budget Director. This position will play a key role in the Institute's budgeting, forecasting, and analysis function. Reporting to the Chief Financial Officer & Treasurer, the Budget Director is a senior administrator and oversees the planning, policy formulation, and implementation of all operational aspects of the Institute's operating and capital budgets. With the assistance of three direct reports, the Budget Director provides oversight of the Institute budget development process and expenditure control activities, tracks year-to-date actuals and provides quarterly updates of current fiscal year forecast to budget, providing high level variance analyses.  The Budget Director collaborates with financial executives in determining operating and capital budget needs and analyzing spending trends and provides oversight of capital spending to applicable fund sources, including Bonds, Gifts and General Budget funds. In addition, the Budget Director provides guidance and training on budget management and financial procedures.   This position must apply advanced budget techniques in analyzing and preparing financial documents and operating budget requests and clearly articulate and explain complex financial data to all constituents. Essential Job Duties Directs the development and administration of the Institute's annual and long-range operating and capital budgets, including budget planning and policy development. Prepares the annual operating budget for General Budget, Gifts and Grants, Endowment, Sponsored Research and Auxiliary fund sources. Develops and updates complex revenue models, including endowment payout, tuition and fees, federal research and indirect costs recovery. Collaborates with Student Affairs and Sr. Leadership in assessing and determining student financial aid budgets and in setting the annual cost of attendance Oversees the budgeting and reporting of faculty and staff salary and benefits; Develops and maintains financial models to determine the cost of the annual salary increase program for general budget and designated funds. Oversees the budgeting and reporting of the annual capital budget including the allocation of spending to the appropriate funding sources (bonds, gifts and general budget).  Collaborates with leadership in Provost Office and Facilities on capital spending plans and funding sources. Acts in an expert advisory capacity and provides strategic overview to senior and executive management on various financial planning initiatives. Develops complex financial models and ad hoc analyses on Institute issues as needed for strategic planning, such as union negotiations. Develops budget presentations for the Board of Trustees. Works closely with leaders of academic and administrative units of the Institute with development of annual and long-range budget and planning processes. Oversees the analyses and reporting of the Institute's budget including developing complex revenue models, analyzing budget requests, assessing the impact of major policy changes, and fiscal and operational issues. Oversees budget variance analysis and reporting.  Regularly reconciles actual revenue and spending against Budget, investigates deviations and prepares financial reports for senior leadership each quarter. Conducts in-depth research and objective analysis of key issues of interest to the Institute; assembles relevant statistics to support diverse budgetary scenarios. Oversight and review of financial or statistical data survey submissions, including but not limited to WASC accreditation, IPEDS, US News and World Report, and National Science Foundation Provides leadership and/or guidance to other personnel (e.g. interviews, orients, trains, assigns and reviews work, counsels and advises, etc.) Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications The successful candidate must have a Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting or a related field. 10 years' experience in financial analysis, budgeting, and reporting. Three years’ experience and knowledge of fund accounting is required A strong knowledge of business and accounting principles is required. Excellent organizational skills, oral and written communication and interpersonal skills, a high level of initiative, and the ability to work in a collaborative environment are also essential. The successful candidate must have the flexibility to work with both conceptual issues and with a high degree of detail and must be able to manage multiple deliverables and deadlines. Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Excel and experience with database tools is essential for this position. Superior verbal and written skills and ability to explain complex financial data to all constituents. A background investigation will be required for this position. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting or related field. Budget experience in a not-for-profit organization with government funding. Experience working with Boards in explaining complicated budget concepts. Required Documents Resume. Cover Letter. Hiring Range $199,000 - $235,000 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10778": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Building and Maintenance Custodian Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Under general supervision, this position will provide support and maintenance to various Athenaeum facilities and grounds and will perform miscellaneous custodial duties as required. This is an Essential Reporting position. In the event of an emergency on campus, an employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery and is expected to report to Campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Provides maintenance services, repairs, rehabilitation, renovation, preventative maintenance, and responds to service/repair calls in a swift and timely manner; performs planned maintenance on various dining and hotel operations equipment. Responds to customer service requests; trouble shoots and diagnoses plumbing, electrical, heating and air conditioning problems. Determines appropriate corrective action, escalates more complex problems to the Hotel Operations Manager and/or Physical Plant. Performs minor plumbing, electrical, heating and air conditioning repairs including faucets, toilets, drain work, garbage disposal, minor carpentry, carpet and furniture repair, door locks, minor interior and exterior painting, minor electrical repairs, replace light bulbs and fixtures and reset circuit breakers. May assist Physical Plant staff in facilities repairs and services. Performs custodial duties in club public areas such as banquet and dining facilities, restrooms, offices and meeting rooms; cleans and polishes floors and carpet, cleans fixtures, cabinets, counters, wash windows. Performs cleaning, sweeping and other tasks in outside common areas and grounds surrounding facility. Performs cleaning tasks in all assigned areas according to prescribed standards of cleanliness and in accordance with Institute and regulatory agencies safety standards and practices. Performs other duties as assigned by the Hotel Operations Manager. Basic Qualifications High school graduate or equivalent with a minimum of 2 years’ experience working in an environment involving facilities or general maintenance, and/or custodial/grounds maintenance. Must have strong verbal and written communication skills Must have a valid California driver's license and maintain it throughout the course of employment. Must be able to adhere to the Institute's motor vehicle policy. Experience and knowledge of basic maintenance services along with exposure and familiarity with one or more skilled trades. Ability to apply general knowledge of basic hand/power tools and equipment. Ability to solve both routine and semi-routine problems. Effective communications skills and the ability to interact with and assist members, guests and other Athenaeum staff. Must be in good health, without physical limitations to perform all duties and responsibilities of the job. Must be able to stand, sit, reach, grasp, squat and bend for extended periods of time; must be able to lift up to 50 pounds on a daily basis such as: lifting and moving tables; maintenance tools; electrical and plumbing supplies, must be able to climb ladders. Applicant must be available to work various shifts, weekends and holidays. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $21.00 - $23.50 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10991": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Business Services Intern Job Category Occasional ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Non-Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. LIGO Laboratory (the Laser Interferometer Gravitational-wave Observatory) seeks a highly motivated and skilled Business Services Intern to join its team. This position is an in-person, year-round internship, located in Richland, WA. LIGO Laboratory is a National Science Foundation major facility dedicated to observing the newly discovered gravitational-wave universe. Jointly operated by the California Institute of Technology and Massachusetts Institute of Technology, the LIGO Laboratory operates world-leading observatories near Richland, WA and Baton Rouge, LA as well as R&D centers on the Caltech and MIT campuses. The LIGO Laboratory’s mission spans a broad and vibrant array of activities related to gravitational-wave physics and astronomy, including detector operations, R&D toward detector improvements, gravitational-wave astrophysics, observatory operations, and education and public outreach. For more information, please visit the Laboratory website at www.ligo.caltech.edu Job Summary This internship provides business students with hands-on experience across multiple business functions within a research environment. The Business Services Intern will support the Business Services Office (BSO) team in areas including procurement, grants management, finance, administration, and operations. This role is designed to offer broad exposure to business functions within a professional setting, providing valuable experience in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. The intern will report to the Business Manager and collaborate with various team members on tasks related to grants management, financial reporting, procurement, government property, and administration. The LIGO Business Office provides comprehensive back-office support across the LIGO Laboratory. The office serves multiple functions—from grants management and accounting to procurement, property and logistics management, and professional communications. This depth of business exposure makes LIGO an ideal environment for interns to gain a well-rounded understanding of how a business office operates and supports a complex research organization. Essential Job Duties The Business Services Intern will: Provide administrative support to BSO team members across various functions Assist with data entry and maintenance of digital records. Support grants management activities and financial reporting processes. Assist with procurement tasks, shipping, and receiving operations. Generate reports and compile data for business office staff. Support government property tracking and administration. Perform general office duties as needed. Other duties as assigned. Learning Objectives Through this internship, students will: Gain exposure to grants and project management, procurement, financial operations, and administrative functions. Learn to use business platforms and software commonly used in professional settings. Develop practical skills in data management, report generation, and file organization. Understand how business services support a research organization. Experience the interconnection between different business functions Skills Development Professional Skills: Time management and prioritization. Written and verbal communication. Teamwork and collaboration. Attention to detail and accuracy. Problem-solving in a professional context Technical Skills: Microsoft Outlook and Office Suite proficiency. Business software and database platforms, including but not limited to DASH360, Oracle, SharePoint, MS Excel. Digital and physical records management. Report generation and data analysis. The Business Services Intern schedule is flexible and can be adapted to suit school schedules. Candidates should be able to work up to 20 hours per week in-person at the LIGO Hanford Observatory. Hours can be adjusted throughout the school year. Basic Qualifications Currently enrolled in an undergraduate or graduate program in business, finance, public administration, Supply Chain Management or similar field. Ability to physically work at the LIGO Hanford Observatory. Reliable transportation to travel to the Observatory location. Excellent written and verbal communication with professional and friendly demeanor. A high degree of organization and attention to detail. Eager to learn, receptive to instruction, with the capability to work autonomously and collaboratively within a team. Takes ownership of assigned tasks and demonstrates a high degree of responsibility and a strong work ethic. Preferred Qualifications Experience in business and report writing software such as Oracle, Dash360, Canva. Working knowledge in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams). Familiarity with other business tools or software is a plus. Required Documents A cover letter summarizing your relevant experience in school or in workplaces and detailing your interest in working at LIGO Lab. Resume. Hiring Range $21.50 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=9841": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Busperson Job Category Parttime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Under direct supervision, the Bus person prepares dining room to service customers, maintains dining room cleanliness and stock levels, provides customer service, and performs basic food and beverage preparation. Performs work in accordance with Institute and regulatory agencies safety standards and practices. The Athenaeum operates 7 days a week. You may be required to work a split shift, overtime, weekends, and holidays as needed. Essential Job Duties Maintains dining room areas, including stocking, set up and breakdown according to protocols. Greets and assists customers; handles and follows up with routine requests. Maintains overall cleanliness and presentation of dining room areas. Buses trays, plates, etc. and cleans tables for upcoming customers. Prepares food bars and/or buffet areas with appropriate food items and supplies as directed. Ensures all drink equipment is clean and working properly. Maintains maximum standards of sanitation and safety. May serve food and beverages to clients per order. May process and post order tickets according to protocol. May have dining room closing responsibilities. Transport equipment such as podiums, tables, and chairs to the dining areas and set in place. Practice the safe handling care and storage of all banquet equipment. Keep the dining room and storage areas clean and always organized. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications Must be able to communicate in English while performing assigned duties. Must be flexible to work a split shift, overtime, weekends, and holidays as needed. Ability to stand for extended periods of time and lift and/or carry up to 50 pounds of tables, dishes, glassware, and food trays etc. California Food Handler’s Card RBS Alcohol Server Certificate Must be able to follow and maintain maximum standards of ServSafe sanitation and safety to ensure the highest standards for food and beverage service. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $20.00 - $23.00 per hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11006": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Campus Custodial Assistant Job Category Fulltime Temporary ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Under direct supervision, applies knowledge of cleaning techniques and performs a variety of custodial duties required to maintain Campus buildings areas clean, orderly, and safe by using hand tools or equipment. Performs work in accordance with Institute safety standards and regulatory agencies (e.g., OSHA, EPA, and CDC guidelines). Essential Job Duties In coordination and cooperation with other crew members, performs cleaning, sanitizing, and disinfecting duties that include, but are not limited to the following: Responsible for following all safety procedures and maintaining a safe and secure work environment. Cleans and maintains floors, including stairwells, by sweeping and wet mopping several types of floor surfaces using hand tools or equipment. Cleans and maintains carpets by vacuuming and spot cleaning carpets and upholstered furniture using tools or equipment. Cleans and disinfects restrooms, showers, kitchens, locker rooms, on a high frequency schedule. Cleans and sanitizes high-traffic public areas and frequently touched sources on a high frequency schedule. Washes and spot clean walls, blackboards, interior windows, light covers, glass surfaces, and elevators. Dusts horizontal and vertical surfaces, which may require working at heights (6’ max) Removes trash by hand or cart and moves trash to designated trash disposal areas. Removes recyclables from building interior and breaks down cardboard boxes. Maintains building entrances and immediate area surrounding building of assignment. Climbs ladders, replace burnt out lights, moves/arranges furniture, and lift/carry items of up to 50 lbs. during the daily assignments. Responsible for the custody of keys in assigned work area; and unlock entry building doors as directed on security building schedule. Must be available to work overtime, including weekends when required. Flexible to perform other custodial duties as needed (Example: Campus Events and Campus Emergency Response). Basic Qualifications At least six months of experience working as a custodian in a fast-pace educational or commercial environment. Ability to communicate and follow verbal and written instructions. Familiar with custodial hand tools, floor care equipment, and cleaning techniques preferred. Must be able to work this assigned work schedule: 5:00AM – 1:30PM, Monday – Friday. Physical Requirements Must be able to lift/carry a maximum of 50lbs. and walk, push, pull, climb, twist, stoop, and bend to accomplish job requirements on a regular basis. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $19.00 - $24.00 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10922": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Campus Custodial Lead Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Under the supervision of a Custodial Supervisor, leads a team of custodians in a research environment. Assist the supervisor in administration of daily operations, and monitors work in progress by applying advance knowledge in all phases of cleaning, sanitizing, and disinfecting processes and floor care techniques. Oversees campus events, projects, and supply distribution. Ensures all custodial duties required to maintain Campus buildings clean are performed in accordance with Institute safety standards and regulatory agencies (e.g., OSHA, EPA, and CDC guidelines.) Essential Job Duties In coordination and cooperation with other Facilities trades and shops, perform various leadership and custodial duties that include, but are not limited to the following: Operates and applies advanced knowledge of floor care techniques and cleaning, sanitizing, and disinfecting techniques, which use specialized equipment or processes in different research environments. Trains newly hired custodial personnel to ensure development requirements are maintain and monitors work in progress. Maintain established standards of performance and perform daily inspections of custodial zone areas. In conjunction with the Custodial Supervisor analyses workflow, provides work schedule recommendations, creates reports, and oversees day-to-day operations. Assumes supervisory responsibilities during Custodial Supervisor’s absence. Inspects and troubleshoots custodial equipment and performs minor repairs as needed. Oversees and monitors personnel on proper cleaning techniques of Campus fountains and filter and backwash techniques. Assists with purchasing, time keeping, evaluations and work scheduling. Responsible for monthly supply inventory and supply distribution. Responds to campus emergencies after hours, assess damages, and prepares reports. Demonstrate ability to work and communicate with all levels of campus personnel. Collaborate with other Facilities Management staff to ensure productivity, consistency, quality, and efficiency expectations are met. Responsible for key control and distribution of work assignments. Assist with management of timekeeping (Kronos) and Work Order (AiM) system daily, which facilitates information for quality assurance and performance measures. Operates vehicles, lift gate trucks, and forklifts, for moving supplies and equipment throughout Campus and off-campus facilities. Must be able to work overtime, including weekends, work any assigned shift when needed to complete projects, and perform all other assigned duties. Basic Qualifications Ability to communicate verbally and in writing with all levels of custodial customers. At least 3-5 years working as a custodian in a leadership position in a fast pace educational or commercial environment. Must be knowledgeable of advanced cleaning techniques and be able to operate different type of floor care equipment. Ability to effectively manage and provide leadership for a large group of employees in a highly diverse environment. Must possess a valid California Driver's license and maintain it throughout the course of employment. Must be eligible to drive Institute vehicles under the Institutes’ Motor Vehicle Use policy and adhere to the policy. A forklift certification or be able to obtain one before employment begins and maintain it throughout the course of employment. Must be able to work assigned work scheduled hours. Schedule 1 (5:00am – 1:30pm – Monday – Friday). Physical Requirements Ability to work at heights and be able to lift 50 lbs. on a regular basis. Ability to walk, push, pull, climb, twist, stoop, and bend to accomplish job requirements on a consistent basis. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $22.25 - $29.25 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10961": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Catering and Projects Assistant Manager Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Catering and Projects Assistant Manager Looking for a non-stop and exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands on, and round-the-clock. If you thrive on teamwork, have a great work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge and innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates four dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, and Avery Kitchen) for a campus community of 2000. We also serve over 950 students, 7 days a week, through our Meal Program and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. This is an Essential Reporting position. An employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery and is expected to report to Campus as soon as possible in an emergency. Job Summary The Catering and Project Assistant Manager is responsible for ensuring daily catering events are successfully set up and executed per event order. They will assist the Catering Manager and Catering Department with events and dining-related assignments. They are responsible for keeping all catering items stocked and on hand as needed. Excellent customer service skills and communication skills are a must. They must possess attention to detail, an eye for design and all things visually pleasing, and an understanding of the necessary logistics for each event at each venue location. They will have a strong ability to coordinate multiple events at the same time and maintain a teamwork mentality that exemplifies ownership and initiative. In addition to catering events, this position will also be tasked with special assignments/projects for the catering department and assist other managers and their departments as needed. Essential Job Duties Oversees schedules, assignments, training, and monitoring of catering coordinators and temporary staffing during, leading up to, and at the end of each catering event. Responsible for efficient and timely event set-up and scheduling of labor side by side with the catering team Provides guidance and training to staff in specific set-up techniques with regard to display, flow, efficiency, and timing. Able to execute catering displays per customer’s themed request and according to client’s level of event (simple, casual, elegant, gala, etc.). Evaluates events, staff, and service performance in order to make improvements and changes were needed. Communicates customer feedback to the Catering. Ensures compliance with all applicable regulatory requirements and maintains the highest standards of sanitation and safety. Ensures employee work areas are ready for servicing customers. Coordinate support staff covering workstations. Maintain Product and Equipment inventory. Communicates effectively, providing clear, direct instructions on work expectations. Maintain a positive relationship with all staff and customers. Must be able to confront a challenge or adverse situation with calm, resolve, and an open, can-do attitude and positive mindset. Cultivates a positive and productive workplace by setting the example with clear communication, vision, teamwork, ownership, and an upbeat attitude. Ability to work varying shifts due to event schedule and department needs including nights and weekends. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications 2+ years of catering experience or equivalent. Demonstrated leadership ability. Demonstrated team-building ability. ServSafe Certification or the ability to obtain certification immediately after hire. Physical ability to lift a minimum of 50 lbs., stand for long periods at a time, move, bend, twist, lift, push, pull, squat, reach, and walk. Ability to complete administrative tasks including invoices, order forms, schedules, audio visual specs, menus, and budgets. Time management skills and ability to work in high-pressure situations. Keen eye for detail with strong multitasking abilities. Proficient computer skills with the ability to communicate well via email, fill out templates, budgets, and order forms. Preferred Qualifications Food and restaurant experience at a high-volume organization or in a university setting. Ability to speak proficient Spanish. Required Documents Resume Hiring Range $23.00 - $27.25 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11094": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Catering Sous Chef Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Looking for a non-stop and exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands on, and round-the-clock. If you have a great team work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge and innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates four dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, and Avery Kitchen) for a campus community of 2000. We also serve over 950 students, 7 days a week, through our Meal Plan and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. Job Summary The Catering Sous Chef reports to the Chef de Cuisine is the primary executor of the culinary vision for Caltech Catering Services.  Works side by side with the Catering Manager when creating menus. Works with the other Sous Chefs and managers to coordinate labor and production for catering events as needed.  Provides recipes, produces food, coordinates staffing, and works on-site for large scale and VIP events, according to business needs. The Catering Sous Chef directs and supervises culinary staff in the production of menus at a variety of Institute venues and is responsible for managing production amounts, ordering product, and managing waste. The Catering Sous Chef will ensure all kitchen areas, equipment, and food handling is conducted according to local health department requirements and regulations.  Responsible for assisting with general functions of kitchen in absence of the Chef de Cuisine. Job Duties Performs full array of cooking skills, to included specialized skills required for certain dishes Creates seasonal menus and menus per client requests and costs them within budget Orders food for daily production based on inventory and projections Provides recipes and efficiently delegates duties to culinary staff well in advance of service dates and/or events Provides management oversight and leadership to the culinary staff and general kitchen team Works closely with the Catering Sales Office to streamline all food related processes, with high attention to detail Checks daily event schedule to ensure that adequate support staff are coordinated May be required to set-up event venue, as needed Ensures sound food costs for revenue generation Works closely with senior management to implement standards, teamwork, processes and practices for improved efficiency, quality, performance, and budget Coordinates staff schedules with the Chef de Cuisine and ensures all food production needs are staffed efficiently Ensures compliance with all applicable regulatory requirements; maintains maximum standards of sanitation and safety Consults with senior management on operational performance, customer needs, and new programs/services Ensures employee work areas are ready for servicing customers; coordinate support staff covering workstations Works closely with other Sous Chefs and assists other units in food production and daily service , as required Attends all meetings as scheduled Provides leadership to other staff to ensure that all food is prepared according to recipes and menu, ensuring kitchen staff have the tools needed for success Conducts staff evaluation and creates improvement plans for culinary team Ensures that all kitchen equipment is in proper working condition Provides coverage for both catering needs and daily output of all programs throughout Dining Services due to high demand and/or shortage of kitchen staff Cultivates a positive and productive workplace by demonstrating, clear communication, strong vision, teamwork, ownership and a can-do attitude Builds a positive relationship with the students and customers by seeking feedback and suggestions Primary work schedule will be Monday through Friday but weekly schedule will fluctuate according to business needs to include evenings and weekends Must assist all other locations when catering calendar is slow As an exempt employee, work hours may exceed 8 hours and/or 5 day work week Must be able to confront a challenge or adverse situation with calm and resolve Ability to communicate clearly and effectively Other duties as assigned Basic Qualifications 5+ years culinary experience in catering Demonstrated leadership ability Demonstrated team building ability ServSafe Manager Certification or the ability to obtain certification immediately after hire Possesses full knowledge and expertise in the use of all food service tools and equipment Ability to provide on-the-job training in food preparation to staff, as needed Physical ability to stand for long periods at a time, move, bend, twist, lift, push, pull, squat, reach, and walk with ease, without injury, and with a sense of urgency and purpose Ability to lift up to 50 lbs Preferred Qualifications Culinary Degree Required Documents Resume Hiring Range 60,200 - 72,000- per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=9281": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Chef de Cuisine Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Looking for a non-stop and exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands on, and round-the-clock. If you have a great team work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge & innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates five dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, Avery Kitchen, and Catering Services) for our campus community. We serve over 950 students, 7 days a week, through our Board Program and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. Job Summary The Chef de Cuisine directs and supervises all Sous Chefs & Cooks in kitchen production for our campus’ food & beverage needs. They will lead a team of Sous Chefs and must have demonstratable culinary management experience, and experience in coordinating multiple production areas efficiently and successfully. The Chef de Cuisine will work as a team member when building, creating, and implementing new menus and menu concepts. Menus will be based on sales, feedback, trends, seasons, and the unexpected. The Chef de Cuisine directly manages three sous chefs to ensure production quality and quantity. Expected to participate in creation of staff improvement plan with the General Manager and be the primary executor of the plan by demonstrating skills to staff, ensuring proper training throughout the kitchen, and supporting staff through the learning process. The Chef de Cuisine. Responsible for supervising staff in set up, production of food, food standards (flavor and presentation) and sanitation of cooking areas. Responsible for managing production amount, ordering food, supervising staff and managing waste. Ensure staff cleans stations at end of shift. Responsible for all functions of kitchen. This is an Essential Reporting position. In the event of an emergency on campus, an employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery and is expected to report to Campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Comfortable with all cooking techniques and able to perform them in high pressure situations. Works closely with Sous Chefs of all units, coordinating menus, purchasing, distribution of labor, and inventory usage. Strong understanding of various dietary restrictions, including food allergies, intolerances and special diets. Will be the primary chef at VIP catering events. Interact with VIP customers and represent Caltech Dining in a positive manner. Knowledgeable about ingredient substitutions to accommodate dietary needs. Experience in creating allergen-friendly menus and adapting recipes to meet specific dietary requirements. Familiarity with food safety practices and cross-contamination prevention in relation to dietary restrictions. Assist in initial staff evaluations and coordinate and consult with leadership on staff improvement plans. Conduct daily staff evaluations; performance will be evaluated on staff improvement. Work closely with the leadership to establish and implement standards, team work, team training, processes and practices where efficiency, quality, performance and cost savings can be improved. Cultivate a positive and productive workplace through communication, vision, teamwork and commitment; reinforcing Dining Services values and beliefs through words and actions. Cultivate a positive relationship with the students, engage with and utilize student feedback. Ensure compliance with all applicable regulatory requirements; maintains maximum standards of sanitation (ServSafe) and safety to ensure the highest standards for food and beverage service. As a senior culinary employee, input is expected on menu direction, customer needs, operational performance, and new programs/services. Responsible for maintaining CDS standards and managing staff to uphold those standards. Other duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications 5+ years of culinary experience. Demonstrated leadership ability. Demonstrated team building ability. Full knowledge of sanitation standards, food borne diseases, and food-borne illness and safety standards. Must be Servsafe certified or have the ability to obtain one. Ability to provide on-the-job training in food preparation to lower-level employees. Physical ability to stand for long periods. Ability to lift 50 lbs. of food products, kitchen equipment, and dining furniture on a regular basis. Minimum 5 years in high volume restaurant or similar setting i.e. catering, banquets, etc. Minimum 3 years on the job management experience. Experience cooking various cuisines including: American, Latin, Italian, Asian, Breakfast, Vegan, Gluten Free, etc. Preferred Qualifications Has or will obtain ACF Chef de Cuisine certification. Working knowledge of menu writing, ordering, labor and cost controls. Required Documents Resume Hiring Range $73.8K - $93.5K per year The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11118": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Contracting Officer Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Exempt Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary The Contracting Officer reports to the Purchasing Contracting Manager and is a key member of the purchasing team. The Contracting Officer performs all the tasks necessary to acquire goods and services for one or more departments/divisions and provides general purchasing and contract administration. Essential Job Duties Handling moderate to complex procurements of supplies, equipment, and services with high financial exposure Communicating with suppliers and internal customers to develop technically sound contracts and/or procurement documents Sourcing, obtaining quotations/bids, making awards, and preparing and issuing purchase orders Monitoring, amending, and closing out standard and declining balance purchase orders Processing and reconciling credit card purchases Preparing competitive and non-competitive procurement justifications Performing cost or price analyses and recommending options that best meet customer requirements Negotiating specifications and terms and conditions and administering procurement contracts Documenting procurement packages to comply with internal and external audit requirements Being a self-starter with the ability to work as part of a team or independently as an individual contributor. Special assignments may include: Developing and issuing solicitation documents, coordinating the evaluation of proposals, and negotiating specifications and terms and conditions Lead project-based work or task teams, including preparing for and leading monthly TechMart training sessions, and speaking or presenting to internal or external customers Participating in Purchasing’s Supplier Relations Committee, which seeks to foster and build relationships among Caltech’s e-procurement catalog suppliers and Campus customers Assisting Procurement’s Systems Analyst in building and generating reports for the purpose of strategic sourcing Responsibility for creating, maintaining and overseeing supplier contracts/master purchasing agreements using Purchasing’s Compliance Contract Tracker tool Basic Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 4 years of purchasing experience OR 6 years of purchasing experience. Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills. Strong customer focus and demonstrated commitment to continuous improvement. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in business administration or equivalent degree. Certified Professional Contracts Manager (CPCM) certification. Certified Professional in Supply Management (CPSM) certification. Experience in higher education. NCMA membership. Experience with government procurement and government property accountability. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $86,700 to $90,000 The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=11033": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Cook - Caltech Dining Services Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Looking for an exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands-on, and round-the-clock. If you have a great team work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge and innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates four dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, and Avery Kitchen) for a campus community of 2,000. We also serve over 850 students, 7 days a week, through our Board Program, and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. Under the direction of the Chef de Cuisine and Sous Chefs, this position requires minimal supervision with proficiency in all areas of culinary services and relies on experience and quick and reasonable judgement to plan and complete assigned tasks. Has experience cooking in a high-volume restaurant or food service facility. Prepares and cooks standard or specialty food items according to recipe using a variety of cooking methods and equipment. Can incorporate substitutions, make adjustments, and understand food portioning and yield. Able to efficiently prepare and fabricate a variety of food ingredients according to recipe standards with speed and good palate. Must be versatile with the ability to learn to work at any food service station. This position should expect location shifts according to business needs. Is responsible for set-up, breakdown, maintaining a clean and organized workspace at all times. Performs work in accordance with Institute and regulatory agency safety standards and practice and performs all job duties as assigned. A positive, can-do attitude and teamwork-ethic are a must. This is an Essential Reporting position. An employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery and is expected to report to campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Performs full array of cooking skills as required for main dishes and side orders. Must work quickly and efficiently within a fast-paced work environment. Prepares and cooks meats, fish, vegetables, gravies, sauces, cereal, soups, fruits, bakery products, and other foods according to recipes or member orders. Cooks from scratch or makes substitutions as requested. Cleans and sanitizes work areas and equipment according to protocol, maintaining clean and organized storage and work areas at all times; deep-cleans equipment and work areas per schedule. Ensures that all kitchen equipment is in proper working condition, informing the managing chefs in the event equipment is not in proper working order. Assists in maintaining timely service for meals and events. Knowledge and understanding of food allergy awareness. Responsible for correct food handling (cook/prep, storage, labeling and rotation) according to Health Department guidelines. Ensures food stations are ready for service and may need to provide coverage for other stations and/or dining locations as needed. Responsible for maintaining all CDS standards and procedures. Cultivates a positive and productive workplace through communication, teamwork, and ownership, attending daily line-ups and department meetings. Greets and serves all guests in a professional, genuine, and friendly manner. Depending on shift, may be required to work some weekends, extended shifts, and overtime. May temporarily work a different shift due to unforeseen events or seasonal high volume event needs. Must be able to confront a challenge or adverse situation with calm, resolve, and an open, can-do attitude and positive mindset. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required or assigned. Basic Qualifications 3 years of experience cooking in a high-volume restaurant or food service facility. Proficient knife skills, ingredient knowledge, cooking skills. Able to work as a member of a team with the ability to take direction with a positive attitude. Flexibility, ownership, and initiative are a must. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Ability to stand for long periods at a time, move, bend, twist, lift, push, pull, squat, reach, and walk with ease, without injury, and with a sense of urgency and purpose. Selected candidate must maintain attendance and arrive on time for all shifts. Must possess a food handler’s certificate or ability to obtain one by the time of hire. Must have the ability to perform basic mathematics: addition, subtraction, multiplication, division and percentage conversion to decimals and count, as related to calculating or converting units of measure for determining proper amounts of food ingredients for large food production. Preferred Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. Knowledge of a variety of regional and international cuisines. 5+ years working in a fast-paced, team environment. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $20.00 - $26.25 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf03/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=CALTECH&cws=37&rid=10848": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Dishwasher - Caltech Dining Services Job Category Fulltime Regular ExemptOvertimeEligible Overtime Eligible Benefits Eligible Benefit Based Apply Now Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute that marshals some of the world's brightest minds and most innovative tools to address fundamental scientific questions. We thrive on finding and cultivating talented people who are passionate about what they do. Join us and be a part of the diverse Caltech community. Job Summary Looking for a non-stop and exciting place to work? Caltech is a world-renowned science and engineering institute harboring some of the world's brightest minds. Our Caltech Dining Services Department (CDS) is in search of hiring and cultivating equally talented individuals who are positive, enthusiastic, and passionate about what they do. We are fast-paced, creative, hands-on, and round-the-clock. If you have a great team work ethic, positive attitude, and are indispensably flexible and quick to adapt to an always changing environment, join us and be a part of this leading edge and innovative community. Our mission is to provide great food, service, and experience for our students and community. CDS operates four dining units (Browne Dining Hall, Red Door Marketplace, Broad Café, and Avery Kitchen) for a campus community of 2,000. We also serve over 850 students, 7 days a week, through our Board Program and maintain a burgeoning Catering Department. Under minimal supervision, this position is responsible for maintaining the cleanliness of all Caltech Dining Services facilities, surrounding areas, including cookware, flatware, and equipment. Has some experience working in a high-volume restaurant or food service facility. Must be versatile with the successful ability to learn to operate all janitorial and ware-washing equipment. Understands they will be required to work at any location and expect location shifts according to business needs. Is responsible for set-up and maintaining an organized, clean, and sanitized station at all times. Performs work in accordance with Institute and regulatory agency safety standards and practice and performs all job duties as assigned. A positive, can-do attitude and team work ethic are a must. The candidate must be flexible, resourceful, and be able to take ownership and initiative in any given task. This is an Essential Reporting position. An employee designated as essential reporting has essential job skills that are needed for response and recovery, and is expected to report to campus as soon as possible. Essential Job Duties Responsible for ensuring exemplary level of cleanliness and sanitation at all dining services locations. Clean doors, windows, sneeze guards, salad bars, drink machines, counters, walls, and all other surface areas that are food service operated and related. Sweep and mop floors, vacuum, empty trash, and keep all areas free of garbage and clutter. Maintain relationships with all kitchen staff to ensure quality of work. Ensure locking of all doors and securing of all equipment (including walk-ins, storerooms, and locker rooms) at end of shift. Inform the managing chefs in the event equipment is not in proper working order. Assist in maintaining timely service for meals and events. Knowledge and understanding of food allergy awareness. Assist in training new cooks and kitchen staff. Understand correct food and chemical handling according to local health department guidelines. Assist with ensuring dining areas are ready for servicing customers. Responsible for the cleanliness and sanitation of food service events. Responsible for maintaining all CDS standards and procedures. Cultivate a positive and productive workplace through communication, teamwork, ownership, and initiative. Greet and interact with all guests in a professional, genuine, and friendly manner. Depending on shift, may be required to work some weekends, extended shifts, and overtime. May temporarily work a different shift due to unforeseen events or seasonal high volume event needs. Must be able to confront a challenge or adverse situation with calm, resolve, and an open, can-do attitude and positive mindset. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required or assigned. Basic Qualifications Experience and knowledge regarding cleaning chemicals and their usage in a food service environment. Customer service oriented. Able to take direction with a positive attitude. Must have effective verbal and written communication skills. Ability to lift a minimum of 50 lbs. Selected candidate must maintain attendance and arrive on time for all shifts. Must possess a food handler’s certificate or ability to obtain one by the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent. 1+ years working in a fast-paced, team environment. Required Documents Resume. Hiring Range $19.00 - $20.75 Per Hour The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. As one of the largest employers in Pasadena, CA, Caltech is committed to providing comprehensive benefits to eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Our benefits package includes competitive compensation, health, dental, and vision insurance, retirement savings plans, generous paid time off (vacation, holidays, sick time, parental leave, bereavement, etc.), tuition reimbursement, and more. Non-benefit eligible employees will have access to some benefits such as onsite counseling and sick time. Learn more about our benefits and staff perks . EEO Statement We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Caltech is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. To read more Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) go to eeoc_self_print_poster.pdf . Disability Accommodations Caltech complies with the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We consider reasonable accommodation measures that may be necessary for eligible applicants and employees to perform the essential functions of a position. If you would like to request an accommodation to complete this application, interview, or otherwise participate in the employee selection process, please contact Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Additionally, if you do not meet the basic qualifications of a role but believe you can perform the essential functions of the job with reasonable accommodation, please reach out to Caltech Recruiting at employment@caltech.edu . Back Share Apply Now"
    },
